# The data of the launch answers before the levels around the code (plan M11 5b; R20: rows, formals, the registry of
# the launch's data, then the lexical levels): the Point of f's data shadows the Point of main, the level around f.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the
# call main().
sub: main () (
    Point: a b
    int: seen 0
)
    fn: f () int (
        Point: a b c
    )
        return: length(Point)
    seen := f()
main()
int: seen main\data\seen
